cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
title: "ALLO: Adaptive Landslide Learning Observatory"
abstract: >-
  ALLO is a research prototype of an early-warning and decision-support system for
  rainfall-triggered landslides on Andean hillslopes, with Manizales (Caldas, Colombia) as its
  initial case. A TypeScript agentic bot orchestrates weather ingestion, a Python (FastAPI)
  stochastic simulation service with an in-process TypeScript failover engine, and a
  language-model layer that explains results but does not compute them. The scientific core
  models latent soil saturation as a rainfall-forced bounded Jacobi (Wright-Fisher) diffusion
  with an exponential hazard link, propagated by seeded Monte Carlo and mapped to four alert
  levels anchored to the 25-day antecedent-rainfall index (A25) of the Manizales early-warning
  system. The repository includes the project model card and an executable regression suite
  that carries the model card's invariants into the user-facing explanation layer.
